    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d72">

                <pb facs="0093" n="81" sameAs="frus:frus1945v05/pg81"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW/4–3045: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Sweden</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stockholm</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-30T15:00:00+01:00">April 30, 1945—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 30—1:03 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1606. British Minister having received instructions in all essential points
                    identic to those in your 782, April 28, 8 p.m.,<anchor n="7" xml:id="d72-f1"/>
                    we called together at 12:30 this morning on Foreign Minister Günther and saw him
                    and Mr. Boheman together. Mr. Günther’s reaction to the request for staff talks
                    as outlined in your telegram was immediately favorable. It was necessary to
                    consult the Government Mr. Günther said but he believed the reply would be
                    favorable.</p>
                <p>I received a telephone call from Mr. Boheman at 2:15 saying that the answer to
                    our <hi rendition="#italic">démarche</hi> is in the affirmative and that the
                    Swedish Government would appreciate our taking action to follow it up as quickly
                    as possible. He suggested that the arrival of the officers who may be sent by
                    General Eisenhower be as unobtrusive as possible and that the Swedish Government
                    would prefer them to be in civilian clothes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d72-f1" n="7" xml:id="d72-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram Noweg 22, April 30, 9 p.m., to the Ambassador to the Norwegian
                    Government in Exile, <hi rendition="#italic">infra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
